  "finalText": "I built the ÉCLAT reveal as a 7-second, 1080×1920 composition on a near-black background (#0A0A0B).\n\n- **Gold line** (`Gold line`): a 1.5 px champagne line (#C9A96E) draws outward from its centre over 2.6 s with Sine In Out, starting at 0.5 s.\n- **Name** (`Name ÉCLAT`): the wordmark is split into five letters, each fading in and rising 18 px with a 0.2 s stagger from 1.6 s. Its tracking starts about 14 px per letter wider and tightens to the resting spacing over 1.6–4.8 s, driven by an expression rather than keyframes.\n- **Subline** (`Subline`): \"EAU DE PARFUM\" in small tracked Inter fades in at 4.2 s in a muted gold.\n- The last motion ends at about 5.4 s, so the lockup holds for the final 1.6 s.\n\nTwo things to know:\n- The serif is a generic `serif` fallback, because Cormorant Garamond isn't installed in the editor. If you can add a licensed display serif, I'll swap it in.\n- The critic's only remaining note asks for more elements. I left it alone, since you asked for a single line and generous negative space.\n\nPossible next steps: slow the whole piece down, add a very slow gold glow behind the line, or export a version with the font you prefer."
